          }
        },
        "text_hrbJbD": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>You've been told these are separate issues. Fix your testosterone. Manage your stress. Take something for blood flow.</p><p>3 problems. 3 solutions.</p><p><strong>But what if they're not 3 problems?</strong></p><p>What if they're 3 symptoms of the same thing?</p><p>It's called <strong>Endothelial Dysfunction.</strong></p><p>Your endothelium is the lining inside every blood vessel. It controls how blood flows — to your muscles, your brain, your dick. Everything.</p><p>After 40 years, that lining breaks down. When it does:</p><p>→ <strong>Blood can't deliver oxygen</strong>. You feel drained. Looks like \"low T.\"<br/>→ <strong>Circulation drops</strong>. Cortisol stays elevated. Stress takes over.<br/>→ <strong>Blood can't reach your erection. </strong>Softer. Slower. Gone.<br/></p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
