        },
        "collapsible_row_YKXiT9": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How fast does it work?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Most guys feel more energy in the first week. Stress drops by week 2-3. Erections improve by week 4-6. Full results by week 6-8.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_pcWg7V": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is this different from Viagra?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Viagra forces blood flow for a few hours. Doesn't fix anything. You need it every time. We repair the blood vessel lining so your body works on its own again. Long-term fix, not a band-aid.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_FbN4r7": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What makes your Shilajit Gummies different?",
            "icon": "quiz",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p><strong>1. Highest Shilajit dose on the market</strong> — 1500mg per serving (10:1 extract). Most brands use 250-500mg.</p><p><strong>2. 75% Fulvic Acid</strong> — The \"delivery molecule\" that makes it absorbable. Most brands don't even disclose their percentage.</p><p><strong>3. SURYA TAPI purification</strong> — Ancient sun-dried method. No chemicals. No heat processing. Preserves full potency, minerals, and vitamins.</p><p>We didn't cut corners. This is the real stuff.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_MVjXh4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How many Shilajit Gummies should I take per day?",
            "icon": "quiz",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Just 2 gummies. That's it.</p><p>Most brands tell you to take 4-5 gummies because their dose is weak. Ours is 1500mg (10:1 extract) — so 2 gummies gives you more than their entire bottle.</p><p>Take them in the morning. Full-day support. Done.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_6iUgcW": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does it have any side effects?",
            "icon": "quiz",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>If taken in large doses, it can cause nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_dRQYEm": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I take this with other supplements? What about medications?",
            "icon": "quiz",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Our Shilajit Gummies are safe to take with other supplements.</p><p>There are no known contraindications with our Shilajit Gummies and any over the counter or prescription medications, though we encourage you to double check with your physician before adding our product to your regimen.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_X9G3Je": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I just eat it? Does it taste bad?",
            "icon": "quiz",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Our Shilajit is 3rd party, lab tested for purity and potency. It has 70% fulvic acid. It has a strong naturally earthy taste that we recommend you mix with warm water, or other liquids like warm milk.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_fXRDM3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is Shilajit Essential Extract safe? Can shilajit interact with medications or existing health conditions?",
            "icon": "quiz",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Shilajit is generally considered <strong>safe for most people when used appropriately.  </strong>However, like any supplement, it's essential to use it responsibly and consult with a healthcare professional before starting, especially if you have any underlying health conditions or are taking medications.</p><p>While shilajit is known for its potential health benefits, it can interact with certain medications or existing health conditions. For example, it may interact with blood pressure medications, diabetes medications, or medications that affect blood clotting. </p><p>Additionally, individuals with certain health conditions, such as kidney disorders, should exercise caution when using shilajit.</p><p>To ensure your safety, it's crucial to discuss any concerns or potential interactions with your healthcare provider before incorporating shilajit into your routine. They can provide personalized guidance based on your individual health status and medication regimen.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
